AOSP Pocket Runtime is an experimental GPL-3.0-only runtime host.

It links Ananbox's Anbox fork:
https://github.com/Ananbox/anbox
The Anbox core retains its original GPLv3 notices, including Simon Fels and
Canonical contributors. Its Android emulator graphics code retains Android
Open Source Project Apache-2.0 notices. Third-party sources and notices are
preserved in vendor/anbox. Consult individual source headers and the lockfile.

PRoot is built from https://github.com/Ananbox/proot under GPL-2.0-or-later,
with the local Android compatibility patch in runtime/proot-android.patch.
PRoot includes contributions from STMicroelectronics and its other authors;
its original COPYING and AUTHORS are preserved in vendor/proot.

Boost 1.83.0 is used under Boost Software License 1.0.
talloc 2.4.1 is used under LGPL-3.0-or-later; original copyright notices and
the LGPL license are included. Exact sources are in sources.lock.json.

The runtime APK bundles the Ananbox AOSP 7.1.1 ARM64 reference guest. This guest
image is an upstream prebuilt, not a locally built ROM. Its source manifest,
reference-image provenance and pinned download are in sources.lock.json.
Guest license notices, including system/etc/NOTICE.html.gz, are preserved in
the bundled filesystem. Manually imported images have their own provenance.
No VMOS executable, library or guest image is incorporated into this runtime.

The separate API 28 integration probe contains selected Android 9 platform
libraries from a pinned redroid/redroid ARM64 OCI image. These are upstream
prebuilts, not locally rebuilt platform libraries. Android 9 license notices
are included as assets/licenses/android9-NOTICE.xml.gz. The image digest and
AOSP header revisions are recorded in sources.lock.json under guest_api28.
The API 28 Binder bridge, guest credential header, property service and native/
Java test programs are built from this project's runtime/api28 sources. The
property service also compiles AOSP android-9.0.0_r61 property-info parser/
serializer sources under Apache-2.0; their copyright notices remain in the
pinned upstream source files. The probe includes the matching upstream ART,
core JNI libraries, boot images and runtime data with the Android 9 notices.
These are bring-up milestones, not a full bootable Android 9 guest.

The API 28 init integration compiles AOSP android-9.0.0_r61 init action, parser,
service, descriptor, rlimit and utility sources with the rootless adaptation
in runtime/api28/init-rootless.patch. Original Apache-2.0 notices remain in
the pinned sources. Compilation uses matching pinned AOSP libc++ headers
(LLVM/University of Illinois and MIT licenses retained upstream). The APK's
Android 9 NOTICE asset covers the corresponding platform runtime libraries.

The API 28 zygote integration compiles AOSP android-9.0.0_r61 app_process,
native Zygote fork hooks and file-descriptor checks from frameworks/base,
adapted by runtime/api28/zygote-rootless.patch. It also statically compiles
ART's sigchainlib with its original exported symbol map. Original Apache-2.0
copyright notices remain in the pinned upstream sources. The development
bootstrap uses the reference image's libopenjdkjvmti.so and Android 9 ART
boot images; their notices are included in the Android 9 NOTICE asset. The
bootstrap, wire-protocol client, Java child and diagnostic log receiver are
project sources under GPL-3.0-only. No VMOS implementation is included.

The separate direct-backend probe contains the same pinned Android 9 linker,
libc, libdl and libm reference prebuilts, covered by its Android 9 NOTICE asset.
Its controlled-call path adapter and native/Java integration tests are project
sources under GPL-3.0-only. PRoot is bundled only for the comparison run; the
direct execution path does not launch or link it. No YLINKER binary or VMOS
implementation is used. The adapter's Linux host tests use the host's libc.

The separate direct platform APK adds matching Android 9 framework resources,
preoptimized system-server code, installer, SurfaceFlinger and Redroid software
EGL/graphics HAL prebuilts from the same pinned OCI layer. Its Android 9 NOTICE
asset covers these upstream components. It includes no PRoot executable.
The direct zygote adaptation is runtime/direct/zygote-system-server.patch.
Pinned AOSP libhidl and libhwbinder headers/IDLs supply the graphics HAL ABI;
original Apache-2.0 notices remain in the fetched sources. IBase headers are
regenerated from that IDL with a host hidl-gen tool. A compile-time enum template
allows a modern host generator with Android 9 runtime headers; it changes no
interface vtable. The in-process software graphics profile is project code.
All guest processes retain the host app's real UID, groups and SELinux domain.
Guest owner/identity metadata is not a security boundary or a host privilege.
The direct system-server experiment adds project-owned health, private storage,
offline network, event-channel and unavailable-audio profiles. Health/manager
headers come from pinned Apache-2.0 AOSP HIDL interfaces. Storage/network
transaction constants are generated from pinned AOSP vold, storaged and netd
AIDL declarations. The unavailable-audio adaptation uses the matching AOSP
AudioSystem declarations and leaves actual service-unavailable results intact.
The matching keystore executable, software Keymaster 3 HAL and selected VNDK
dependencies are upstream prebuilts from the same pinned Android 9 image,
covered by its NOTICE asset; they are not locally source-built platform claims.
